  "answer": "No past ticket reports this problem. PowerToys#48725 has a similar symptom (a context-item shortcut acting twice), but it traces the cause to both CommandBar and ContextMenu handling TryCommandKeybindingMessage. It does not involve LocalKeyboardListener or HC_NOREMOVE hook notifications. PowerToys#48096 is about the global activation hotkey needing two presses, which is also a different issue. Treat this as a new bug: the proposed fix is for LocalKeyboardListener to process only HC_ACTION notifications and ignore HC_NOREMOVE peeks. Adding repro steps (which shortcut, and what happens when it fires twice) would help the team confirm it."
